DS precedent (curated in the generator, drift-gated against source). file_impact updated to name the generator explicitly. AC2's 'test fails when a verb is added without classification' is served by two independent checks: render() raises when the curated key set != rebar._cli._CONFIRM_SCOPE (so the CI drift gate fails), plus a direct assertion in tests/unit/test_mutation_confirmations.py.","timestamp":1787186612771596001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation complete locally, all three residuals:\n1. AC1 (reduce path): new structural block in tests/unit/test_mutation_confirmations.py spies the SHARED seam (_confirm.emit/emit_text) and asserts, per verb, exactly ONE routed line and stdout == that line + newline (nothing printed outside the seam) — parametrized over create/link/transition, plus a no-op-path variant (link re-link, transition already-at-status). Proved it is a real guard by mutation: replacing confirm_created's emit_text with a bare print makes create fail with 'routed 0 lines through the shared seam'. The event reducer was deliberately NOT the spy target: rebar.reducer.reduce_ticket is re-exported by binding the function object at import time (rebar.reducer.__init__, rebar._native, rebar.__init__), so a call-count on the defining module would silently under-report. The 'no follow-up store read' half is instead proved by test_confirmation_formatters_need_no_store, which formats create/comment/tag-noop/transition lines with cwd in an empty tmp dir and REBAR_ROOT deleted — no store exists to read.\n2. AC2 (verb inventory): curated MUTATION_VERBS in scripts/gen_cli_reference.py (17 rows = _WRITES_FULL | _LIFECYCLE), each with noop flag + condition, rendered as a 'Verb inventory: no-op-capable vs always-writes' table in the generated docs/cli-reference.md. Drift-gated two ways: _check_mutation_verbs() makes render() raise when the key set != rebar._cli._CONFIRM_SCOPE (so the CI drift gate fails on an unclassified verb), and test_an_unclassified_verb_fails_the_generator asserts that behaviour directly by deleting a row.\n3. AC3 (old->new mapping): same curated rows carry old/new columns, rendered as the 'Confirmation-line record (pre-42cd70b889 -> today)' table. Old strings were read out of git (42cd70b889^), not paraphrased: notably transition printed 'UNBLOCKED: <ids|none>' on a CLOSE ONLY and was silent on every other target, which is why reopen (a delegation to transition closed->open) was silent before.\nNOTE ON THE DOC: docs/cli-reference.md is GENERATED; it was regenerated with 'python scripts/gen_cli_reference.py', not hand-edited. Gates: make lint PASS (complexity active=49 new=0 increased=0 stale=0), make typecheck PASS (572 files).","timestamp":1787187356353471001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed to Gerrit: change 1933 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1933), commit 5581841317, Change-Id Ib5a41001770a785ddcdca1a9b141a0ea8f5ca54c, 3 files / +382 -1. Local evidence before push: make lint PASS, make typecheck PASS, full tests/unit 5077 passed / 7 skipped (the single ERROR in test_compact_all_selection was its own repo-HEAD-moved guard firing because I committed while the suite was running; re-ran that file clean, 17 passed). Awaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1; not submitting and not closing until both are green.","timestamp":1787188089869576001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"AC evidence (kept in this comment, not the description, so the plan-review attestation stays current — ticking a box is attestation-safe, adding prose is not):\nAC1 — seam-spy on _confirm.emit/emit_text in tests/unit/test_mutation_confirmations.py, parametrized over create/link/transition: exactly ONE routed line per dispatch and stdout == that line + newline (nothing printed outside the seam), plus a no-op variant (re-link, already-at-status transition). Proven to bite: replacing confirm_created's emit_text with a bare print makes create fail 'routed 0 lines through the shared seam'. test_confirmation_formatters_need_no_store covers the no-follow-up-store-read half by formatting with cwd in an empty tmp dir and REBAR_ROOT unset.\nAC2 — MUTATION_VERBS in scripts/gen_cli_reference.py, 17 rows == _WRITES_FULL | _LIFECYCLE, rendered as the 'Verb inventory: no-op-capable vs always-writes' table in the generated docs/cli-reference.md. _check_mutation_verbs() makes render() raise on drift from rebar._cli._CONFIRM_SCOPE (so the CI drift gate fails on an unclassified verb); test_an_unclassified_verb_fails_the_generator asserts that behaviour by deleting a row.\nAC3 — 'Confirmation-line record (pre-42cd70b889 -> today)' table in docs/cli-reference.md from the same curated rows; old strings read out of 42cd70b889^ rather than paraphrased.\nAC4 — make lint PASS (complexity active=49 new=0 increased=0 stale=0), make typecheck PASS (572 files), full tests/unit 5077 passed / 7 skipped. Gerrit change 1933 merged as 0c1906abc9 with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, 0 unresolved comments. One non-blocking review advisory (already marked resolved by the bot): the 'stdout carries nothing the seam emitted' invariant has a documented exception on link's REDIRECT path, which the merged test test_link_redirect_record_is_byte_identical_and_sole_stdout_result covers and this new test deliberately does not exercise.","timestamp":1787190191592982001}],"created_at":1786816265484764001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"4bd9a550-5098-47de-a449-21c17540ff8c","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"6bda-9d58-8546-4638"},{"link_uuid":"5932f4eb-c300-445b-abcc-4ac10ae2c88b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"042d-8428-d999-4fd5"}],"description":"## Why\nClosing satiated-unrideable-tapeworm (Gerrit 1809, merged 42cd70b889) left three residual sub-clauses that are test/reporting hardening, not behavior gaps — all behavior is merged, tested observable-behaviour-style, and CI-green. This ticket carries the remainder so the parent could close honestly.\n\n## Scope (from the parent's AC1-AC3 residuals; full tables in the parent's close-out comment)\n1. AC1 residual: add call-count/monkeypatch assertions on the shared confirmation reduce path so a future regression that bypasses the shared seam (printing per-verb again) is caught structurally, not just per-verb by exact-line tests.\n2. AC2 residual: ship the verb inventory table (no-op-capable vs always-writes) as generated or hand-maintained documentation (docs/cli-reference or a test-enforced table), so the no-op contract is enumerable.\n3. AC3 residual: record the per-verb old→new confirmation-line mapping (the parent's comment has the full table) in docs or the test suite as golden data.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [x] Reduce-path structural assertion exists (call-count or seam-spy) covering at least create/link/transition.\n- [x] Verb inventory (no-op-capable vs always-writes) lives in a durable, reviewable location and a test fails when a verb is added without classification.\n- [x] Old→new mapping table recorded in docs or golden test data.\n- [x] make lint / make typecheck clean; lands via Gerrit.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/test_mutation_confirmations.py","reason":"Add the reduce-path seam-spy/call-count assertions (create/link/transition) and the test-enforced completeness check for the verb classification + confirmation-line migration tables."},{"path":"scripts/gen_cli_reference.py","reason":"docs/cli-reference.md is a GENERATED artifact (CI drift gate); the verb inventory and old-to-new confirmation mapping are curated here and drift-gated against rebar._cli._CONFIRM_SCOPE, following the existing INTERCEPT_COMMANDS precedent."},{"path":"docs/cli-reference.md","reason":"Regenerated output carrying the n